# Your Task

1.  Clone the "cs4457-wireless-dist" branch of the git repository (same as used in AIMD1).

2.  Look at the simulation of a wireless networking scenario with four nodes, where
    node 1 transmits to node 2 and node 3 transmits to node 4.

    The simulation has various parameters affecting the data rate transmitted and
    the wireless network configuration.

    In this assignment, we'll be measuring the total number of bytes received
    by nodes 2 and 4.

3.  Your goal is to manipulate
    the position of the nodes to be most advantageous for particular network configurations.

    Update the `SetupPositions` function so that:

    *  (--mode=1) at least 150% more bytes are received when using

            --mode=1 --physicalMode=DsssRate1Mbps --sendRate=0.9Mbps --rtsCts=false --txPower=10

       compared to

            --mode=1 --physicalMode=DsssRate1Mbps --sendRate=0.9Mbps --rtsCts=false --txPower=16

    *  (--mode=2) at least ____ more bytes are received when using

            --mode=2 --physicalMode=DsssRate1Mbps --sendRate=0.45Mbps --rtsCts=false

       compared to

            --mode=2 --physicalMode=DsssRate2Mbps --sendRate=0.45Mbps --rtsCts=false

       AND at least 0.1Mbps are received in both scenarios

    *  (--mode=3) at least 200% more bytes are received when using

            --mode=3 --physicalMode=DsssRate1Mbps --sendRate=0.45Mbps --rtsCts=true

       compared to

            --mode=3 --physicalMode=DsssRate1Mbps --sendRate=0.45Mbps --rtsCts=false

    *  (--mode=4) at least 130% more bytes are received when using

            --mode=4 --physicalMode=DsssRate1Mbps --sendRate=0.9Mbps --rtsCts=false

       compared to

            --mode=4 --physicalMode=DsssRate1Mbps --sendRate=0.9Mbps --rtsCts=true

    *  (--mode=5) at least ____ more bytes are received when using

            --mode=5 --physicalMode=DsssRate2Mbps --sendRate=0.45Mbps --rtsCts=false

       compared to

            --mode=5 --physicalMode=DsssRate1Mbps --sendRate=0.45Mbps --rtsCts=false

# The simulation

`scratch/wireless-ex.cc` implements a simulation of a wireless scenario with 4 nodes.
